# tfvars can hold environment-specific values that aren't meant for git even though
# terraform.tfvars.example (bootstrap) and the environments/*/terraform.tfvars
# committed in this repo are deliberately just defaults, not secrets — this guards
# against someone later adding a *.auto.tfvars with real values.
*.auto.tfvars

